Additional workarounds for stdexec with nvcc 12.8 and a GCC 13 host compiler.

The original nvcc workarounds allow parsing HPX's execution headers, but sender
instantiations still fail in nvcc's generated host code. This incremental patch
addresses callable non-type template parameters, unintended cv/ref qualifiers,
virtual diagnostic types, GCC copy elision, and references to constexpr global
function objects from host/device functions. A dependent sync_wait alias is
spelled through a helper to preserve its result type in generated host code.

Use STDEXEC_DEMANGLE_SENDER_NAMES consistently in HPX and its consumers; it
selects a different sender representation. HPX's Stdexec interface target
exports this definition for nvcc builds. These workarounds enable host-side
sender machinery in CUDA translation units, not arbitrary GPU sender execution.

With the complete patch stack, nvcc 12.8.93 and GCC 13.3 crash with
"Segmentation fault" when compiling this CUDA translation unit without
STDEXEC_DEMANGLE_SENDER_NAMES:

  #include <stdexec/execution.hpp>
  #include <tuple>
  int main() {
    auto r = stdexec::sync_wait(stdexec::just(42));
    return r && std::get<0>(*r) == 42 ? 0 : 1;
  }

Compile with -std=c++20 --expt-relaxed-constexpr --extended-lambda and the
patched include directory. Adding -DSTDEXEC_DEMANGLE_SENDER_NAMES makes the
same program compile and run. The macro selects a descriptor object instead
of a lambda descriptor; it must not differ between C++ and CUDA consumers.

Per-header rationale and diagnostics (with the representation macro enabled):

- __basic_sender.hpp: the original connect object produces "identifier
  stdexec::connect is undefined in device code". Construct the same stateless
  callable locally under nvcc.
- __just.hpp: likewise, __make_sexpr<just_t> is undefined in device code.
- __receivers.hpp: likewise, __invoke and set_value are undefined in device
  code. Preserve the original expressions for other compilers.
- __sender_adaptor_closure.hpp: likewise, __apply is undefined in device code.
  Only nvcc uses the internal __tup::__apply_t spelling.
- __meta.hpp: without cv/ref removal, completion_signatures<...> const&
  "is not a class, struct, or union type" during completion deduction.
- __sender_concepts.hpp: without cv/ref removal, then reports "deduced return
  type does not satisfy placeholder constraints", followed by no operator|.
- __utility.hpp: reference callable template arguments produce "no instance
  of function template stdexec::connect_t::operator() matches the argument
  list" in sync_wait, followed by its incompatible-connect static assertion.
- __sync_wait.hpp: the dependent value_type alias produces generated host
  errors including "_Error was not declared in this scope". The helper keeps
  that type lookup dependent.
- __config.hpp: enable the existing GCC copy-elision workaround for nvcc's
  GCC host compiler too; see https://gcc.gnu.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=98995.
- __diagnostics.hpp: retain the nonvirtual diagnostic fallback for nvcc's
  constexpr virtual type handling. The config and diagnostics hunks were
  not independently triggered by the bounded just/then/variant regression;
  retest the wider HPX/Kokkos consumers before removing them.

Tracking: https://github.com/TheHPXProject/hpx/pull/7711. No separate stdexec
issue is recorded for these additional failures. When updating the pin,
retest the reproducer and the stdexec_cuda/algorithm_sender_cuda regressions
with each workaround disabled before removing it. The preceding async_scope
patch separately tracks NVIDIA/stdexec#2304.

Keep this patch separate so existing FetchContent checkouts with the earlier
nvcc patches can acquire it. It applies to stdexec commit
04de75de5807e73a229acf047c6976575e313359, pinned by HPX 2.0.0-rc1.

